---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Subscribe from '../components/Subscribe.astro';

/** What's next. `now` marks the step in progress, shown in bold. */
const next = [
  { when: 'Early October', what: 'Development builds, open source' },
  { when: 'Late October', what: 'Marfa 0.1, the first semi-stable release', now: true },
  { when: 'Early November', what: 'The Mac and iOS apps with early testers' },
  { when: 'Late November', what: 'Public TestFlight, Marfa Cloud in testing, and the full website' },
];
---

<Base
  title="About Marfa"
  description="Why Marfa exists, how it was rebuilt this year, and what’s next: Marfa 0.1, TestFlight for the Mac and iOS apps, and Marfa Cloud."
>
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p>
    Marfa grew out of a frustration. After trying more apps than I can count, every switch meant leaving something
    behind. It also draws on experience with customer data platforms, where one well-modelled source of data is the
    whole point.
  </p>
  <p>
    That matters more now that agents can build an app in an afternoon. Apps can come and go; the data underneath
    should last, and make sense to whatever reads it next.
  </p>
  <p>
    Marfa has been rebuilt more than once this year. It began as a hosted service that tried to be compatible with
    everything, which pulled it away from what mattered most: a sound data model and a server you can rely on. So it
    became something you run yourself, with a Rust core under its command-line tool and native apps. Marfa Cloud will
    follow as an optional relay for reaching it from anywhere, without holding your data.
  </p>
  <p>
    It’s a personal project, not a business. It ships when it works, not before. Marfa is free and open source, so anyone
    can run it, build on it or take it somewhere new.
  </p>

  <h2>What’s next</h2>
  <ol class="next">
    {
      next.map((step) => (
        <li class:list={{ now: step.now }} aria-current={step.now ? 'step' : undefined}>
          <span class="when">{step.when}</span>
          <span>{step.what}</span>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>

  <h2 id="follow">Follow along</h2>
  <p class="lead">
    Marfa is being shaped with a small group of early testers. Leave your email to hear as the apps open up and new
    things ship.
  </p>
  <Subscribe />
</Base>

<style>
  /* Rows are padded rather than spaced, and the list pulls up by the same
     amount, so the first row sits where the heading's spacing puts it. */
  .next {
    --row: 6px;
    margin: calc(var(--row) * -1) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    font-size: var(--small-size);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .next li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 8.5em minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 12px;
    padding: var(--row) 0;
  }

  .when {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .now {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .now .when {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .lead {
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    font-size: var(--small-size);
  }

  #follow {
    scroll-margin-top: 24px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .next {
      --row: 4px;
    }

    .next li {
      grid-template-columns: 7.4em minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 10px;
    }
  }
</style>
